Surely some reference to The Pirates of Penzance about the
Keystone Kops-ish characters there would be appropriate,
and something suitably obscure on February 29th about how
old the PC _really_ is. The "Poor Wandering One" song seems
like a fit to the life of the adventurer, too.

Something from Sherlock Holmes? Perhaps a Speckled Band
headgear or waistcoat, or a dog that doesn't bark in the
night, could be worked into NetHack.

Ravens who peck out your eyes should honor Poe with a
"you'll see me ... nevermore" message.

An adventurer trying to pile up treasure in heaps is just
_ripe_ for a Scrooge McDuck reference, maybe when zapping
a wand of polymorph at a pile of loot.

A second attempt to purchase food in a delicatessen should
get back from the shopkeeper "Oh, so it's "more Sir", is it?"
to honor Dickens.

A few Get Smart references could be fun.

Bones files could honor various fossil hunters, particularly
the Leakey family, with "Lucy" quotes or random tombstones.

On All Hallows' Eve, instead of a full moon, warn about the
Great Pumpkin rising, to honor Skippy.

A level like the Rogue level, with one of the more obscure
universes Calvin told Hobbes his Dad had convinced him existed,
would be cute.  "Everything here seems to be in black and white",
e.g., or a Spaceman Spiff reference.

When the PC applies the Bell, Book, and Candle, surely a
reference to the cat Piawacket should occur, from the movie
of that name.

